# Obelisk ISO package set.
#
# Phase 1 scope: a live medium that boots to a text console under both BIOS and UEFI.
# The desktop (Plasma 6), the installer (Calamares), and the Obelisk packages arrive in
# later phases. Every name below was verified against archlinux.org/packages; nothing
# here is guessed.
#
# Decision D1 (docs/ARCHITECTURE.md): the Windows compatibility layer, the VM stack,
# graphics drivers, and codecs are deliberately NOT on this medium. The first-run
# wizard fetches them after install. That is what keeps the ISO inside 3.5 GB and out
# of the way of the licensing rules in docs/LEGAL.md.

# --- base system -----------------------------------------------------------
base
linux
linux-lts
linux-firmware

# --- initramfs -------------------------------------------------------------
mkinitcpio
mkinitcpio-archiso
mkinitcpio-nfs-utils

# --- boot loaders ----------------------------------------------------------
# syslinux serves BIOS, grub serves UEFI. See bootmodes in profiledef.sh.
syslinux
grub
efibootmgr
edk2-shell

# --- memory diagnostics ----------------------------------------------------
# The boot loader configuration inherited from releng references both of these, and
# mkarchiso warns when a referenced entry has no package behind it.
#
# Adding them rather than deleting the entries, for two reasons. They cost 144 KiB
# compressed in total (71927 + 71853 bytes), which is nothing against a 3.5 GB budget.
# And Obelisk explicitly targets hardware Windows 11 rejects, where failing RAM is a
# common and frequently misdiagnosed fault, so a memory tester on the medium earns its
# place for this audience more than for most distributions.
#
# The alternative was surgery on inherited configuration files that Phase 2 deletes
# anyway, which is fragile work with a short shelf life.
#
# OPEN DECISION for Phase 4: the boot menu specified for the product has exactly five
# entries and memtest is not among them. Phase 4 owns the menu and must decide whether
# memtest becomes a deliberate sixth entry or these two packages come back out. Recorded
# in TODO-VERIFY.md so the choice is made rather than inherited.
memtest86+
memtest86+-efi

# --- filesystems -----------------------------------------------------------
# btrfs-progs is not optional: the whole unbreakability model in Phase 6 is Btrfs.
btrfs-progs
dosfstools
e2fsprogs
exfatprogs
f2fs-tools
xfsprogs
ntfs-3g

# --- partitioning ----------------------------------------------------------
gptfdisk
parted

# --- networking ------------------------------------------------------------
networkmanager
wireless-regdb

# --- installation tooling --------------------------------------------------
arch-install-scripts
pacman-contrib

# --- console usability -----------------------------------------------------
# The live console must be usable before any desktop exists, and terminus-font is
# what makes a HiDPI console readable at all.
terminus-font
nano
less
sudo
which
